{"id": "EUVD-2026-92043", "enisaUuid": "c659b05d-23e8-3fef-aa06-9e2a3100337f", "description": "W (vincent-peugnet/wcms) through 3.18.0 contains a remote code execution vulnerability that allows authenticated editors to write arbitrary files by abusing the unvalidated path in POST /api/v0/media/upload/[*:path]. Attackers can upload .php files executed by the web server, use encoded ../ sequences to write outside the media directory, and delete arbitrary files via DELETE /api/v0/media/[*:path].", "datePublished": "2026-10-03T22:30:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-05T14:16:25", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vincent-peugnet/wcms/issues/662", "https://github.com/vincent-peugnet/wcms", "https://github.com/vincent-peugnet/wcms/blob/cda5bcdb95dbdb1e804fdfe0e5fd2e2b2f8a90e2/app/class/Controllerapimedia.php#L24-L44", "https://github.com/vincent-peugnet/wcms/blob/cda5bcdb95dbdb1e804fdfe0e5fd2e2b2f8a90e2/app/class/Media.php#L98", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/w-wcms-through-3.18.0-rce-and-arbitrary-file-write-via-media-upload-api"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r3hg-hgx7-58g9", "CVE-2026-105123"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f097b02a-b7af-39f1-874c-67b1ad061af3", "product": {"name": "wcms", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.18.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "af01c498-cf91-3a36-b1d3-45799f38349c", "vendor": {"name": "vincent-peugnet"}}], "isExploited": false}